# The request and response of OpenMower's slic3r_coverage_planner/PlanPath, field by field, so whatever
# calls OpenMower's planner today can call this one (the MowBite Planner's ~/plan_path).
# Fill, lane direction, spacing, loop offset and loop count come from the request, everything else (turn
# radius, K-turns, lane order, waypoint spacing, max_path_poses) from the node's parameters. Without a
# usable plan the response has no paths.

# lanes
uint8 FILL_LINEAR=0
# loops further and further in
uint8 FILL_CONCENTRIC=1

uint8 fill_type
# rad, lane direction in the map frame, 0 = +x, counter-clockwise
float64 angle
# m, lane spacing (OpenMower's tool_width)
float64 distance
# m, how far the first perimeter loop runs inside the outline (OpenMower's outline_offset, usually 0)
float64 outer_offset
# perimeter loops along the outline and around every obstacle
uint8 outline_count
# the lanes reach this many loops further out
uint8 outline_overlap_count
bool skip_area_outline
bool skip_obstacle_outlines
bool skip_fill
geometry_msgs/Polygon outline
geometry_msgs/Polygon[] holes
---
# The perimeter loops as one path (is_outline 1), the lanes with their turns and the drives between them
# as another (is_outline 0). Each path is continuous, poses 0.1 m apart (parameter waypoint_spacing),
# facing the next one. A path longer than max_path_poses goes on in the next one, from its last pose.
Path[] paths
